      "message": "This packet doesn\u0027t look like a valid ethernet frame any more: it\u0027s too short:\n\nA runt frame is an Ethernet frame that is less than the IEEE 802.3\u0027s minimum length of 64 octets [note: includes 4 byte CRC, aka FCS]. Runt frames are most commonly caused by collisions; other possible causes are a malfunctioning network card, buffer underrun, duplex mismatch or software issues.\n\nIt may or may not be zero (or garbage) padded by the kernel and/or nic driver/fw/hardware, and it may or may not be dropped by the network...",
      "revId": "b9d8f6218f65249464ef40c6ad5bb754166309d0",
